From 0ac3bfa6d099916cc58fc258db17221801f49d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noahwang <234082230@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:52:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(py36): restore dual-runtime settings lost in R1 master
 syncs

R1 merge 04af2db3d04 dropped the proctoring de-duplication, the CMS
HEARTBEAT_ELASTICSEARCH_TIMEOUT import and the submissions
MIGRATION_MODULES; 4dbe0c68497 reverted the course wiki include. On
fd5e359ec1c the LMS check fails on Python 3.6 and the CMS check fails on
both runtimes.

- Plugin apps already in INSTALLED_APPS are skipped, so edx-proctoring is
  installed once whether it comes from the static list (Python 2.7 fork,
  no entry point) or also from its 1.5.x plugin entry point (Python 3).
- The wiki include uses only the (patterns, app_name) pair that both
  django-wiki pins return.
- The submissions migration snapshots match edx-submissions 2.0.12 and
  2.1.1 except for byte-string literals.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
